course: dictionary
lesson: 9016
title: One word, two meanings: skirt
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives skirt as a noun, which is a piece of clothing, and as a verb, which means to go round the edge of something. Context tells you which one is meant. In «a pleated skirt» and «a school skirt», skirt is clothing.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. In «Alice jumps up in such a hurry that she tipped over the jury-box with the edge of her skirt», the skirt is the clothing she wears. When the verb is used, the sentence shows a path or a person going round something. Always check by putting your meaning into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
explain: Skirt can also mean avoiding something. To skirt round a problem or question means to avoid talking about it. Words like issue, problem or question are the clues. A hard topic is not a piece of clothing, so the meaning is different here.
fact: Skirt can be a noun (a skirt, skirts) or a verb (skirt, skirted, skirting).
fact: A skirt is a piece of clothing worn by women and girls that hangs from the waist and has no separate legs.
fact: To skirt something means to go round the edge of it.
fact: To skirt round a problem means to avoid talking about it.
fact: A skirting board is a strip at the bottom of a wall.
exercise: «A Station Road boy calls Maddie a boy in a skirt.» What is a skirt? | To talk about a hard topic | *A piece of clothing that hangs from the waist with no separate legs | A strip at the bottom of a wall | A path that goes round a hill
exercise: «The walkers skirted the lake to reach the village.» What does skirted mean? | Jumped over | Swam straight across | Sat down to rest | *Went round the edge of
exercise: «The minister skirted the question about the money.» What does skirted mean here? | *Avoided talking about it | Wrote it down | Asked the question again | Answered it fully
test: «The skirting board needed a fresh coat of paint.» What is a skirting board? | A path round a lake | A piece of clothing | *A strip at the bottom of a wall | A type of paint
test: «Mum asked why I skirted the question about my homework.» What does skirted mean? | Read it aloud | *Avoided it | Copied it out | Answered it clearly
exam: «The path skirts the cliff edge, so take care.» What does skirts mean? | Hides behind | Climbs straight up | Falls off | *Goes round the edge of
